    "missing": [
      {
        "what": "Parameter counts per model are derivable from the text (3L(n+1)+mJ+2 with n=6, mJ=1, i.e. 3, 24, 45, 66, 87, 108, 129). Rows say 'not stated'.",
        "locator": "Sec. IV.B, Sec. V.A, Fig. 6 caption",
        "versions": "V5"
      },
      {
        "what": "The authors' argument that MSE is non-increasing in L by construction (nested parameter spaces, Eq. 26). This explains monotonicity but not a power-law form.",
        "locator": "Sec. VI.A, Eqs. 25–26",
        "versions": "V5"
      }
    ],
    "verdict_notes": "Evidence for V5 is thin: six points, fewer than one decade, fit 'to guide eyes' only. MSE is inferred from the acceptance ratio via MSE=(log⟨A⟩)^2 rather than measured on held-out data. Monotonic decrease is partly guaranteed by the nested-initialisation training scheme. No uncertainties are reported."
  },
